{center}{arialbld}The Island of Doctor Nikloz{arial}


{arialbld}The Katzaro-Nikon War:{arial}

A narrow body of water, {arialbld}the Sea of Karal{arial}, is all that separates the immense steppes of {arialbld}Katzarin{arial} from the volcanic archipelago of {arialbld}Nikondo{arial}. Nevertheless, the two cultures which grew out of these environments could not be more different.{pause}

1000 years of proximity were not enough for the {arialbld}Paranos{arial} of Katzarin and the {arialbld}Fanatos{arial} of Nikondo to find some kind of common ground outside the battlefield.{pause}

This November morning the Katzar fleet once again crossed the Karal Sea, simultaneously attacking the Nikonese capital and the main islands of the archipelago. After a heavy bombardment, a flood of carriers drenched the Nikonese beaches with artillery and tanks annihilating the Fanato defenses.{pause}


{arialbld}Geo-Cultural Notes:{arial}

{arialbld}Katzarin:{arial} Ruling over a territory of some 90 million km2, the {arialbld}Parano Coalition of Greater Katzarin{arial} unites 59 ethnic clans under the iron hand of {arialbld}Fédor Kharkan{arial}, an omnipotent oligarch: {arialbld}the Katzar-Khat.{arial}{pause}
Dating from an archaic tradition, this title can only be won by a clan chieftain, or Khatman, each year at the spring equinox. The candidate must challenge the Katzar-Khat in single mortal combat by any weapon with a blade. In 14 years Fédor Kharkan has slain 23 ill-advised hopefuls.{pause}
 
{arialbld}Nikondo:{arial}The {arialbld}Fanato{arial} Empire counts some 19 million Nikonese venerating the Emperor Hiro-Hiro Tagamoshi "the Innovator", last heir to a thousand-year-old feudal society.{pause}
Eager for new technologies, the Nikonese acquired from Portugreek merchants in the 16th century the compass, which allowed them to break their isolation and push their domination beyond the seas. Skillful and industrious craftsmen, the Fanatos built up over a time a fleet of unequalled power. The Admiral of the Imperial Fleet assumes the role of Commander of Nikonese Forces, his name is {arialbld}Fujiro Goziya{arial}.{pause}


{arialbld}Duty of Assistance:{arial}

The Emperor Tagamoshi is instituting numerous reforms aimed at progressively phasing out his country's feudalism. The president of the Federation of Schyzo States, Clarissa Audrey Jackson, sees in him a benevolent sovereign open to democracy. An agreement of Anti-Katzar assistance was concluded in the presence of General Tyron Spirex.{pause}

In addition, our information service suspects Katzarin of having secretly conceived terrible weapons of a chemical nature. This would be the work of a Psycho scientist known as {arialbld}Doctor Nikloz{arial}, who has obtained from  Katzarin an unlimited budget to pursue his sinister activities.{pause}

{arialbld}YOUR MISSION:{arial}

You must lead our troops into the Meridian Ocean to retake the Fanato Islands conquered by the Katzars. Then you must land in Katzarin so as to discover and annihilate their construction complex of these abominable chemical weapons.
{}
